
== decimal and integer: arithmetic works in both orders ==
d + i                              3.5
i + d                              3.5
d - i                              -0.5
i - d                              0.5
d * i                              3.0
i * d                              3.0
d / i                              0.75
i / d                              1.33333333333333333333333333
d % i                              1.5
i % d                              0.5
the result is always a decimal     decimal
integer / integer stays an error   false

== decimal and integer: ordering works in both orders ==
d < i                              true
d <= i                             true
d > i                              false
d >= i                             false
i < d                              false
i > d                              true
2.00d <= 2i                        true
2.00d >= 2i                        true
big integer 9223372036854775807i > 1d true

== equality is strict about types ==
2d == 2i                           false
2d ~= 2i                           true
2d == 2                            false
2i == 2                            false
rawequal(2d, 2i)                   false
convert first: 2d == decimal.create(2i) true
2d <= 2i and 2d >= 2i              true

== decimal and number: never implicit ==
d + n                              error: attempt to perform arithmetic (add) on decimal and number
n + d                              error: attempt to perform arithmetic (add) on number and decimal
d * n                              error: attempt to perform arithmetic (mul) on decimal and number
d / n                              error: attempt to perform arithmetic (div) on decimal and number
d % n                              error: attempt to perform arithmetic (mod) on decimal and number
d < n                              error: attempt to compare decimal < number
n <= d                             error: attempt to compare number <= decimal
-n then + d                        error: attempt to perform arithmetic (add) on decimal and number
d == n (just false)                false
convert explicitly                 3.5
or go the other way                3.5

== decimal and strings: no coercion either ==
d + '1'                            error: attempt to perform arithmetic (add) on decimal and string
'1' + d                            error: attempt to perform arithmetic (add) on string and decimal
d .. 'x'                           error: attempt to concatenate decimal with string
'x' .. d                           error: attempt to concatenate string with decimal
d < '1'                            error: attempt to compare decimal < string
tostring first                     x1.5

== decimal and booleans, nil, tables ==
d + true                           error: attempt to perform arithmetic (add) on decimal and boolean
d + nil                            error: attempt to perform arithmetic (add) on decimal and nil
d + {}                             error: attempt to perform arithmetic (add) on decimal and table
d == nil                           false
d == {}                            false
not d                              false
d and 'yes' or 'no'                yes
0d is truthy                       truthy

== the library accepts integers wherever it accepts decimals ==
decimal.add(1i, 2i)                3
decimal.min(3i, 2.5d, 4i)          2.5
decimal.max(3i, 2.5d, 4i)          4
decimal.floor(7i)                  7
decimal.lt(1i, 1.5d)               true
decimal.le(2i, 2.00d)              true
decimal.scale(7i)                  0
decimal.add(1, 2d)                 error: invalid argument #1 to 'add' (decimal expected, got number)
